  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "correctness",
    "affected_api": "cvxpy.reductions.complex2real.canonicalizers.matrix_canon.lambda_sum_largest_canon",
    "observed_behavior": "Before the fix, lambda_sum_largest_canon doubled k unconditionally, so a real symmetric argument was rebuilt with 2k on the original n\u00d7n matrix. In the PR reproducer the solver returns 30.0 with lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) == 20, which violates the constraint lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) <= 5. When 2k > n the atom can also yield spurious unboundedness.",
    "expected_behavior": "The optimal value should be 7.5, matching the same problem solved without the unrelated complex variable z. k should be doubled only when the argument has an imaginary part.",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "lambda_sum_largest is applied to a real symmetric matrix (e.g. X = cp.Variable((3,3), symmetric=True))",
      "The problem also contains an unrelated complex expression (e.g. z = cp.Variable(complex=True) with cp.abs(z) <= 1), so Complex2Real runs over the whole problem",
      "k = 2 with n = 3, so 2k > n",
      "Solved with cp.CLARABEL"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "X = cp.Variable((3,3), symmetric=True); z = cp.Variable(complex=True); p = cp.Problem(cp.Maximize(cp.trace(X)), [cp.lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) <= 5, X >> 0, X << 10*np.eye(3), cp.abs(z) <= 1]); p.solve(solver=cp.CLARABEL)",
        "buggy_output": "30.0 (with lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) == 20, constraint violated)",
        "expected_output": "7.5",
        "value_kind": "float",
        "source": "PR#3376 reproducer (pr_body)"
      },
      {
        "input": "Test test_lambda_sum_largest_real_arg applied to unpatched master (6a"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": []
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": "places=4 in test_lambda_sum_largest_real_arg (assertAlmostEqual on reference 7.5 and on result vs ref); assertLessEqual lambda_sum_largest(X,2).value <= 5 + 1e-4",
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Mathematical property violated: lambda_sum_largest(X,k) constraint should hold, i.e. sum of k largest eigenvalues of a real symmetric matrix must be preserved; bug doubled k (2k) for real arguments in Complex2Real, so the constraint lambda_sum_largest(X,2) <= 5 was violated",
      "Before fix: objective 30.0 with lambda_sum_largest(X, 2) == 20, violating the constraint <= 5",
      "After fix: optimal value 7.5, matching the same problem without the unrelated complex variable z",
      "Spurious unboundedness occurs when 2k > n (here 2k=4 > n=3 would arise under the bug)",
      "The fix moves real.k *= 2 inside the imag_args[0] is not None branch so real arguments are not doubled; the divide-by-two and 2n x 2n Hermitian dilation apply only to complex arguments",
      "Problem setup: X = Variable((3,3), symmetric=True), z = Variable(complex=True), objective Maximize(trace(X)), constraints lambda_sum_largest(X,2) <= 5, X >> 0, X << 10*I, abs(z) <= 1; solver CLARABEL",
      "Regression test test_lambda_sum_largest_real_arg in cvxpy/tests/test_complex.py asserts reference 7.5 and equality with and without z"
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "Bug only manifests when the problem contains an unrelated complex expression; without z the buggy path is not triggered",
      "Benchmark tables in discussion passages are unrelated timing data and do not provide numerical correctness evidence",
      "Pre-fix value 30.0 is stated in the PR body only, not in the test",
      "Solver tolerance for CLARABEL is not stated beyond the test's places=4 comparison"
    ]
  },
